# Burning-Tree Shaman: "Whenever a player activates an ability that isn't a mana ability, this creature deals 1 damage to that
# player." Any player, any object's ability, wherever it is: on turn 2 Bot2 activates Ajani Resolute's 0 (a loyalty ability): the
# trigger is above the 0 (Stack.Count = 2) and resolves first, Bot2 at 19 before the life gain puts him back at 20. On turn 3
# Bot1 activates his own Figure of Destiny: the Shaman's controller is a player too (Bot1 at 19). On turn 4 Bot2 forestcycles
# Generous Ent from his hand (an ability of a card in a hand still counts): 19. Every land and Mox tapped for mana here leaves
# the life totals alone: the card excludes mana abilities (CR 605.1a): the engine emits a mana ability's activation too (CR 605.3), and the trigger
# asks `is_mana_ability` of it and refuses.

